The hook body — invoked by the provider, not usually by a human

Usage: cs sessions hook run [OPTIONS] --event <EVENT> [PAYLOAD]

Arguments:
  [PAYLOAD]  The provider's payload. Codex passes it as this trailing argument; Claude pipes it on stdin, which is read when this is absent

Options:
      --config <PATH>    Path to the state directory (default: the galaxy's .cosmon/state/)
      --event <EVENT>    Which moment fired: `session-start`, `turn-start`, `turn-end`, `waiting`, `asking` or `answered`
      --provider <NAME>  The pilot this hook runs inside: `claude` or `codex`. The payload is not consulted, so a Codex hook passes `codex`; `claude` otherwise
  -v, --verbose          Enable verbose output
      --json             Output in JSON format
      --session <SID>    This session's cosmon id. Defaults to `$COSMON_SESSION_ID`
  -h, --help             Print help
